{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"- i don't like the idea that we're implanting artificial strings like `## User (${actor.display})` throughout. i'm guessing there are a lot of these that were placed throughout this project without me realizing it while vibe-coding? i get that it adds context for the model to understand what's happening but imo at the same time we should be avoiding taking these models OOD, especially nowadays that they're getting RL'ed inside their respective harnesses. that's kinda contradictory to our whole effort which is literally putting the context history adn even thinking tokens of some models into others ig so do push back against me, but i feel like we should be developing a happy medium between the two concepts that involves minimal non-necessary additions\n- ok i think my claude->codex->opencode->claude point may have been misinterpreted. yes 0-20claude, 21-35codex, 36-50opencode and then we resume that in claude ok i'll stick with your example numbers. my point is that on the first resumption, the 0-20 opening into codex, the code current does things like add those `## User (${actor.display})` lines or input claude's thinking trace as raw convo text into codex even though codex uses encrypted thinking traces since we don't know how to encrypt accordingly. those mutations then get carried into the opencode resumption which presumably does its own mutations. then, when we finally want to resume into claude again, instead of resuming the original claude thinking inside the thinking data point, presumably we're now resuming it into claude's own convo window with the text-demarkated `<thinking>` or whatever it is we input. i imagine these mutations over the course of resumptions could get gross, which you've already pointed out with the multiple back-to-back cumulative thinking strings. so my point is, when resuming, should we be resuming the data into claude exactly as opencode experienced it, or should we be resuming 0-20 in the original claude-native format, then 21-35 from teh original codex data rather than the edited-by-resumption-inside-opencode data? ah yeah sorry i thought you hadn't understood but it seems you settled on it with \"render each turn from the conversation where that turn originated\". trouble now is, is this even doable given our data structure? like cledger records the whole resumed ugly convo, so we'd have to notice that 0-20 and 21-35 are dirty adn go find their original source if available; do we currently have those pointers? also, jic the info is lost, we'd need to fall back to whichever is what, oldest?\n1. in theory this \"human at hop 3 actually saw the folded text and may have replied to it\" is really only an issue for the \"<thinking>\" tags and similar, whereas the actual core _content_ shouldn't be much if at all different, no? yeah i agree removing the fold markers (i was referring to them as \"<thinking>\" tags and similar previously). \n2. when ancestors aren't available i wouldn't bothe rwith a loud disclose message, it's just distracting adn not that big of a deal. but yeah unwrapped heuristics being the fallback is much better than the mechanism.\n3. oh yeah ancestral import notices make sense, especially since they'd help the model not go crazy if we really mess something up since it'd have context as to why its hsitory feels mesed up. \n- yeah definitely prefer my generic facility. should we drop a todo handoff doc into turnbridge to have another agent get that done or do it ourselves from here?\n- yeah do we eventually nned to make turnbridge gemini & qwen aware? not super urgent we can just add a todo for me to hadnle later","type":"text"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"defab1d48ffb334ef077b543c74110f5a05efd71","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:60ec7095-