{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_011jmU7HLvkS4T7eHZS4n6Vv","input":{"command":"cd ~/repos/evintunador/turnbridge-worktrees/policy-split && cat > docs/TODO_HANDOFF.md <<'EOF'\n# Handoff and TODO\n\nSpun out of [POLICY_SPLIT.md](POLICY_SPLIT.md) and\n[LINEAGE_AND_COMPOUNDING.md](LINEAGE_AND_COMPOUNDING.md), 2026-08-13. Items are\nsplit by whether the design is settled enough to hand to another agent.\n\n---\n\n## A. Ready to hand off: cledger generic extension facility\n\n**Repo:** `conversation-ledger`. **Depends on nothing here.**\n\n### Problem\n\ncledger's extension point today is \"`kind` is an open string\n(`src/schema.ts:7-9`) and `content` is never interpreted.\" That is real and\nturnbridge uses it correctly — `recordContinuation` appends a `continuation`\nevent through the public `appendEvents`. But it is **ungoverned**: any two\nproducers can pick the same kind name, and a consumer parsing another tool's\n`content` is coding against an undocumented, unversioned shape.\n\nThis became concrete when context-graph's design took a dependency on\nturnbridge's `continuation` payload (`rel:\"continues\"`, `imported_through_seq`).\nintent-recall is the likely third. A private convention that two other tools\nparse is a public interface with no owner.\n\n### Explicitly NOT the fix\n\nDo **not** add `continues`, `continuation`, or any bridging concept to\ncledger's own vocabulary. cledger must not become aware of turnbridge — it\nwould be documenting a relation it has no use for and cannot validate the\nmeaning of, and it inverts the dependency. The facility must stay agnostic\nabout what any third-party kind *means*.\n\n### Scope\n\n1. **A namespacing convention for third-party kinds and link rels** — e.g.\n   `turnbridge/continuation` — so independent producers cannot collide.\n   Decide whether it is enforced (validation rejects an unnamespaced\n   non-`KNOWN_KINDS` kind) or conventional (documented, warned about).\n   Enforcement is a breaking change for anything already writing bare custom\n   kinds — turnbridge's `continuation` is exactly that, so a migration or\n   grace path is needed.\n2. **Optional payload validation for registered kinds.** A producer registers\n   `{ kind, schema }`; `finalizeEvent`/`validateEvent` enforce the shape\n   without cledger interpreting it. Keep it opt-in — an unregistered kind must\n   still be storable, since \"store what you don't understand\" is the existing\n   contract (`unrecognized`, `raw`).\n3. **Documentation** in cledger's design doc: what the extension point\n   guarantees, what it does not, and who owns a namespace.\n\n### Constraints to respect\n\n- Custom kinds must remain storable without registration.\n- Do not change `eventId`'s identity subset — `kind` is already in it, so a\n  rename from `continuation` to `turnbridge/continuation` changes every\n  existing event's id. That is the migration hazard; treat it as the main\n  design risk, not an afterthought.\n- Reading must stay tolerant: an unknown namespace is not an error.\n\n---\n\n## B. Stays with us: still design-entangled\n\nNot ready for handoff — each is blocked on a decision in the companion docs.\n\n- **Per-turn origin rendering** (LINEAGE_AND_COMPOUNDING §3, §3a). Blocked on\n  the as-recorded vs. as-it-would-have-been call, and on adding\n  `source_event_ids` to the `continuation` payload first, without which the\n  walk cannot resolve a turn to its origin precisely (fabrication breaks\n  positional correspondence three ways).\n- **Marker reduction** (POLICY_SPLIT §4, and the six-marker inventory). The\n  one unambiguous win available now: opencode's `reasoning` parts are\n  plaintext, so `[visible thinking]` should not be injected on the opencode\n  path at all — it can carry a native reasoning part. Claude and Codex cannot\n  (unforgeable signature / ciphertext).\n- **Move human-facing disclosure out of the transcript into `plan.notes`**,\n  which already prints to the terminal and never enters model context. Applies\n  to model substitution, ancestor-unavailable, and size reporting. The import\n  notice is the one disclosure that genuinely belongs in context.\n- **Probe whether Claude's `system` / `attachment` line types reach model\n  context** (`docs/specs/claude-session-format.md:74`, `:196`). The two specs\n  disagree: claude-session-format calls attachments \"purely informational, not\n  needed for resume\"; cledger's `context_injection` describes them as material\n  inserted into the model's context. If they do reach context, the import\n  notice stops being a counterfeit user turn.\n- **Read `producer.model` / `producer.provider`** instead of `actor.id`\n  (LINEAGE_AND_COMPOUNDING §1). Independent of everything else, small, and\n  strictly better input for opencode's provider resolution, which currently\n  guesses by string-splitting the model id.\n\n---\n\n## C. TODO for Evin: Gemini and Qwen awareness\n\n**Not urgent. Live but untested as of cledger 0.21.0.**\n\ncledger 0.21.0 added `gemini-cli` and `qwen-code` capture adapters. turnbridge\nconsumes it via `file:../conversation-ledger`, so this is already in effect.\n\nWhat happens today, unverified:\n\n- Those conversations **appear in the picker**. `listConversations` has no\n  source filter — `conversations.ts:72` takes `producer.source` verbatim.\n- They render with a **raw source label**, since `cliLabel` falls through to\n  the bare string for unknown names (`types.ts:21`).\n- They can be **bridged out of** but never **into**: `buildPlan` native-resumes\n  only when `target.name === summary.source` (`resume.ts:109`), which can never\n  match, so they always fabricate. `parseCliName` also rejects them as target\n  arguments.\n\nSo bridging *out* of Gemini/Qwen may already work as a free feature — a source\nneeds no adapter, only a target does — but it is silently one-way and has never\nbeen exercised. Decide whether to (a) verify and document it as supported,\n(b) add real target adapters, or (c) filter unsupported sources out of the\npicker until one of those happens.\nEOF\ngit status --short && echo \"--- verify resume.ts:109 ---\" && sed -n '109p' ../../turnbridge/src/resume.ts","description":"Write handoff/TODO doc and verify a citation"},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"defab1d48ffb334ef077b543c74110f5a05efd71","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:60ec7095-598e-476f-acb7-dd4ee0cab6f1","seq":343},"id":"ev1-707055d263d202b5840bf8bf8152e90a0914b53591ab538c828b8c51f4748198","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-19T02:04:19.730Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"60ec7095-598e-476f-acb7-dd4ee0cab6f1","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.235","tool":"cledger","version":"0.22.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_011jmU7HLvkS4T7eHZS4n6Vv","input":{"command":"cd ~/repos/evintunador/turnbridge-worktrees/policy-split && cat > docs/TODO_HANDOFF.md <<'EOF'\n# Handoff and TODO\n\nSpun out of [POLICY_SPLIT.md](POLICY_SPLIT.md) and\n[LINEAGE_AND_COMPOUNDING.md](LINEAGE_AND_COMPOUNDING.md), 2026-08-13. Items are\nsplit by whether the design is settled enough to hand to another agent.\n\n---\n\n## A. Ready to hand off: cledger generic extension facility\n\n**Repo:** `conversation-ledger`. **Depends on nothing here.**\n\n### Problem\n\ncledger's extension point today is \"`kind` is an open string\n(`src/schema.ts:7-9`) and `content` is never interpreted.\" That is real and\nturnbridge uses it correctly — `recordContinuation` appends a `continuation`\nevent through the public `appendEvents`. But it is **ungoverned**: any two\nproducers can pi