{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01RCF45LusLAoHxenQBGjjcM","input":{"content":"---\nname: turnbridge-worktree-convention\ndescription: \"Feature work for turnbridge goes in ../turnbridge-worktrees/, keeping the main checkout on main\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nEstablished 2026-08-11 at evintunador's request: turnbridge feature work lives\nin git worktrees under `/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge-worktrees/`\n(sibling to the repo, one directory per branch), so the main checkout stays on\n`main` and stays usable. Not `.claude/worktrees/`, the harness default.\n\n    cd ../turnbridge\n    git worktree add ../turnbridge-worktrees/<branch> -b <branch>\n\n**Why it matters here specifically:** the global `turnbridge`/`tb` command is\nnpm-linked to the main checkout (`npm ls -g` → `turnbridge@x -> …/turnbridge`),\nso whatever branch that directory has checked out is what the user's CLI runs.\nDoing feature work in the main checkout silently swaps the tool they use. That\nis exactly what happened on 2026-08-06: the opencode fix sat on a branch in the\nmain checkout, so `tb` was fixed only while that branch was checked out.\n\nTwo gotchas, also written into `../turnbridge-worktrees/README.md`:\n- Each worktree needs its own `npm install && npm run build` — `conversation-ledger`\n  is a `file:` dep resolved relative to the checkout and `node_modules/` is not\n  shared.\n- A worktree's build never reaches the global `tb`; run its own `node dist/cli.js`\n  to exercise it. See [[turnbridge-mvp-decisions]].\n","file_path":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-turnbridge/memory/turnbridge-worktree-convention.md"},"name":"Write","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"defab1d48ffb334ef077b543c74110f5a05efd71","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},